  "text": "NCCIH Consumer Guide: Herbs at a Glance & Safety Considerations | Publisher: National Cent\nCommon Natural Products & Evidence Status\nOverview of common dietary products: - Ginger: Evidence supports ginger\nfor mild nausea related to motion or pregnancy. Use in moderate food-level\namounts. - Chamomile: Commonly used as tea for mild relaxation. Caution in\nindividuals allergic to ragweed. - Peppermint Oil: Enteric-coated\npeppermint oil may ease mild IBS symptoms. Avoid unformulated raw oil\ningestion.\nPage 2 of 4 | Official Educational Resource",
